  [engine] lfphys.core.cosmology.flrw: the core holds ΛCDM (w = −1, constant density); w0–wa is a phenomenological extension beyond ΛCDM. The data disagree: Planck 2018 with BAO and supernovae is consistent with Λ (w0 = −1.028 ± 0.031 at wa = 0), DESI DR2 BAO + CMB prefers w0 > −1, wa < 0 at 3.1σ (2.8–4.2σ with supernovae): the question is open
