  [p01_gravity] the interval from t = {t:.6g} s recomputed with the accuracy parameter η = {eta2} instead of {eta}: the largest difference of the positions {dx:.3g} au, as a fraction of the system's size, estimates the computation's error on the interval (the step ∝ √η: with η/2 it is √2 times shorter, and the error of the 4th-order scheme about 4 times smaller, measured {lo}–{hi})
